<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">29 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">4 events that happened on 29 November, from 1530 to 1963.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1530">1530 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">496 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cardinal Wolsey dies on his way to face treason charges</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Thomas Wolsey, once <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>'s all-powerful Lord Chancellor, died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leicester">Leicester</a> Abbey. He had fallen from favour after failing to obtain the annulment of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry</a>'s marriage to Catherine of Aragon.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/colorado" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/colorado.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1864">1864 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">162 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Colorado troops massacre Cheyenne and Arapaho at Sand Creek</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Colonel John Chivington's volunteer cavalry attacked a peaceful camp at Sand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colorado">Colorado</a>, killing about 150 to 200 people, mostly women, children and the elderly. Congressional inquiries condemned the attack.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1947">1947 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">79 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The UN votes to partition Palestine</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The UN General Assembly adopted Resolution 181, recommending separate Jewish and Arab states with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> under international control. Fighting broke out the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Johnson sets up the Warren Commission</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Lyndon Johnson appointed a commission under Chief Justice Earl Warren to investigate Kennedy's assassination. Its 1964 report concluded that Lee Harvey Oswald acted alone.</p></div></li></ol>
